KG42.register("source_edge_archive-718969d23c718df77c885873",{"id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R019::E::v141-c-R019-E002","paper":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation","rule_id":"v141-c-R019","rule_ref":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R019","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R019-E002","source":"bidding.supply","target":"pricing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R019-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-08"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R019-C001"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"COMP-c0cbb067ee5d581a","target":"COMP-f276c683eb055d9b","source_occurrence_id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R019::V::bidding.supply","target_occurrence_id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R019::V::pricing.local","source_unit_id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-a-M03::bidding.supply","target_unit_id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-a-M03::pricing.local","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"BS internal buying-price calculation over the scheduling horizon. | BS internal selling-price calculation over the scheduling horizon.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-08"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"1aeb7a4066a0823dcdb511f4118f0ebc15ba558c9160358fc51c2e92337e71b4","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M03","source_definition":"The coordinator limits supply-bid updates by evenly randomly selecting a predefined-size set of participants forbidden to change their energy bids at each iteration. Scope: Optional bid-count step length control in iterative P2P energy bidding; selection covers all participants and applies to supply bids among their submissions. Condition: Bid-count control is adopted; the supply bid belongs to a participant selected into the forbidden set. The coordinator must reject a supply bid whose change exceeds the prescribed ramping-rate limit. Scope: Proposed practical coordinator enforcement of optional bid-ramping control in P2P energy bidding. Condition: The proposed enforcement rule is adopted and a supply bid exceeds the prescribed ramping-rate limit. SDR supply bids follow the energy-bid content specification in Formula (A18), derived from the participant's decision-making-model results. Scope: Supply quantities represented within SDR energy bids during the iterative bidding process. Condition: The energy bid is negative at the relevant time step. Supply-bid changes at each iteration must respect the prescribed ramping allowance around the previous bid, with the resulting bounds clipped to the minimum and maximum energy-bid limits. Scope: Supply energy-bid constraints in the simulation's iterative decision-making model. Condition: The bid-ramping form of optional step length control is adopted. The two controls may be combined by first limiting the number of bids allowed to change and then limiting changes to the allowable supply bids. Scope: Supply-bid updates under optional combined step length control. Condition: Bid-count control and bid-ramping control are used together.","target_definition":"Submitted negative net-energy quantities enter the internal selling-price calculation through the horizon sums specified by the BS pricing model. Scope: BS internal selling-price calculation over the scheduling horizon. Submitted positive net-demand quantities enter the internal buying-price calculation through the horizon sums specified by the BS pricing model. Scope: BS internal buying-price calculation over the scheduling horizon.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R019-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Submitted negative net-energy quantities enter the internal selling-price calculation through the horizon sums specified by the BS pricing model. Scope: BS internal selling-price calculation over the scheduling horizon.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-08"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g07-ev-08","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p27-c2r2__v141-a-M03-pricing","page":27,"printed_page":"1019","section":"A.2.3","anchor_text":"(A27) r agent under mid-market rate mechanism. energy cost and income evenly throughout the time hor","equation_id":"A28","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-27.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Bill sharing is a mechanism in which all the prosumers share the energy cost and income evenly throughout the time horizon. The energy bids required by the BS mechanism are the same as those in the SDR mechanism as described by Formula (A18). The internal price is calculated by\n\n\\begin{cases} p_t^{buy} = r_t^{retail} \\cdot \\frac{\\sum_{t \\in T_u^+} \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{n,t}^{bid}}{\\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} \\sum_{t \\in T_l^+} e_{n,t}^{bid}}, & T_u^+ = \\{ t \\mid \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{n,t}^{bid} > 0, t \\in T \\}, T_l^+ = \\{ t \\mid e_{n,t}^{bid} > 0, t \\in T \\} \\\\ p_t^{sell} = r_t^{export} \\cdot \\frac{\\sum_{t \\in T_u^-} \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} |e_{n,t}^{bid}|}{\\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} \\sum_{t \\in T_l^-} |e_{n,t}^{bid}|}, & T_u^- = \\{ t \\mid \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{n,t}^{bid} \u003c 0, t \\in T \\}, T_l^- = \\{ t \\mid e_{n,t}^{bid} \u003c 0, t \\in T \\} \\end{cases}  (A28)\n\nFormula (A28) actually distributes the total energy cost and income of the whole energy sharing region among the prosumers according the amount of energy they consume and generate. Taking the buying price part as an example, r_t^{retail} \\cdot \\sum_{t \\in T_u^+} \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{n,t}^{bid} is the total energy cost of the whole region for importing electricity from the retailer throughout the time horizon, which is divided by \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} \\sum_{t \\in T_l^+} e_{n,t}^{bid}, the sum of each individual prosumer's total positive net energy consumption throughout the time horizon."}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"BS internal buying-price calculation over the scheduling horizon. | BS internal selling-price calculation over the scheduling horizon.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-08"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R019-E002","source":"bidding.supply","target":"pricing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R019-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-08"]},"paper_scope_note":"SDR, MMR, and BS are kept separate; the A18 net quantity differs from the A24 independent component; optional step-size control and the divergent loop in the example are not treated as general convergence or necessary dependencies."}});
